<title>CANADA: Canada government cash balances fall in week.</title>
<headline>Canada government cash balances fall in week.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-05-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The government of Canada's cash balances fell in the week that ended April 30, the Bank of Canada said on Friday.</p>
<p>				    Wk to Apr 30 Chg on wk Chg on yr</p>
<p>Notes in circulation		  27.35   +0.427    +0.984</p>
<p>Government cash balances	     4.84   -1.339    +2.146</p>
<p>Govt securities outstanding	462.46   -0.422    +2.858</p>
<p>Treasury bills			 131.70   -0.400   -30.800</p>
<p>Canada savings bonds		  32.76   -0.021    +2.080</p>
<p>All figures in billions of dollars.  </p>
<p>					   Mar 97     Feb 97     Mar 96</p>
<p>M1					  68.17	68.43	59.02</p>
<p>M2					 391.83     392.57     389.03</p>
<p>M3					 506.01     500.30     475.88</p>
<p>Note - Figures are unadjusted, in billions of dollars.</p>
<p>   Chartered bank assets			 Mar	   Feb</p>
<p>   Net foreign currency			-16.69	-19.81</p>
<p>   Canadian dollar			     705.60	692.96</p>
<p>   Total Canadian liquid assets	    108.03	105.87</p>
<p>((Reuters Ottawa Bureau (613) 235-6745))</p>
</text>
